{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/443244-mystery-of-the-dominion","id":443244,"title":"Mystery of the Dominion","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-15T16:32:42-07:00","id":443244,"title":"Mystery of the Dominion","content":"So, when the playtest document for the Ordo Dracul's new mechanics in Secrets of the Covenant came out, I was pretty excited that Wyrm's Nests got some attention. However, there were a few things that were missing; Fontal Rituals, for instance (they were never the best, mechanically, but I loved the thematics behind them). Rather than coming up with some new type of mechanic altogether, though, I decided I would work with what's already there; Mysteries of the Dragon.<br /> <br /> With that, I spent a few hours on this (so yes, it's likely got some mistakes or oversights, was a quick job). The idea behind the Mystery of the Dominion is for those that study it to better utilize Nests to improve upon their own condition. And as a bit of a nod to Fontal Rituals, I've converted some of them into either Coils or Scales, and have noted that the Scales of the Dominion are themselves often called &quot;Fontal Rituals&quot;. I also slipped the &quot;Mind of the X&quot; merits from the first edition covenant book in there, too, in a different form.<br /> <br /> Obviously, when the actual book comes out this might need updating, but in the meantime, let me know what you all think!<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1XPW_0RPHBjqRHCpzYL6HMRF7Ax26oEVky5_aeCq4lW4/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":1130,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","user":"falco1029","date":". 03-15-2015, 07:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T18:10:31-07:00","id":443451,"title":"","content":"Gut reaction feedback, I like the Coil in concept, but it needs some refinement. I expected more focus on empowering a specific Nest, and less all around nestness. :<br /> <br /> <i><b>Mind of the Devouring Wyrm</b></i><br /> Seems alright at first glance, a bit of an investment. I wonder if the returns aren't a touch low, though that depends on the number of nests they possess. Also, the name is kinda janky, and doesn't immediately evoke to me that the vampire can now better attune to Nests.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Eyes of the Dragon</i></b><br /> Being able to sense out Nests is nice, but I wonder about the utility of it. Strictly speaking only in very specific instances would I expect a character to run across a whole ton of nests. I'd take an alternative approach, extending the vampire's kindred senses throughout the nest she has claimed.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Arcane Blood</b></i><br /> Much too strong, this basically removes the need to hunt entirely. At the very least I'd limit it to once a week, or better tie to to existing feeding. Something like, &quot;When the vampire feeds she draws additional power from the nest. The first [nest dots] points of damage she deals while feeding yield double the vitae. She can benefit from no more than [Nest Dots] additional vitae in this way each week.&quot; <br /> That changes the power from 'vampire never leaves nest' to 'vampire invites people into her nest' while makes for more interesting narrative possibilities.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Lair of the Beast</i></b><br /> I'd shift the lair buffing functions of dot two here. Give the vampire what is essentially a lair frenzy, that causes the entire Nest to side with him (increasing all relevant Nest pools by his Blood Potency). That puts more focus on the whole &quot;my nest is better than yours&quot; and avoids crossover with the Coil of the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Master of the Domain</i></b><br /> I like it generally, but wonder if there isn't a way to differentiate it from Animalism 5 (which has many of the same effects).<br /> <br /> <b><i>Scales</i></b><br /> On the whole I like all of these. The first one struck me as strange, but strange is the dominion of scales. Love the procedures too, they nailed the whole &quot;crazed sorcerer's evil house&quot; feel I expected of the Mystery. Bravo there.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T20:01:41-07:00","id":443653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/443244-mystery-of-the-dominion?p=443451#post443451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gut reaction feedback, I like the Coil in concept, but it needs some refinement. I expected more focus on empowering a specific Nest, and less all around nestness.</div> </div> </div> </div>The way the Ordo works, to me, seems like they'd be more about improving themselves all around, not getting better with one nest as a Coil investment. The focus on an individual nest would depend on their Nest Guardian merit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i><b>Mind of the Devouring Wyrm</b></i><br /> Seems alright at first glance, a bit of an investment. I wonder if the returns aren't a touch low, though that depends on the number of nests they possess. Also, the name is kinda janky, and doesn't immediately evoke to me that the vampire can now better attune to Nests. </div> </div> </div>I'll admit, I just took the old merit name, but I guess it doesn't necessarily fit as well as I'd hoped it did. I'll switch it. As for low returns, do you have any suggestions for something else to add on or tweak it to? One thing that comes to mind is to say -all- their nest merits are considered one higher (when applicable), and maybe any attached Safe Place or Haven, too?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><i>Eyes of the Dragon</i></b><br /> Being able to sense out Nests is nice, but I wonder about the utility of it. Strictly speaking only in very specific instances would I expect a character to run across a whole ton of nests. I'd take an alternative approach, extending the vampire's kindred senses throughout the nest she has claimed. </div> </div> </div>That's why I had doubled up on the benefits there. Maybe if I add on an ability to use kindred senses to learn more about the nest, gather more details, and improve his kindred senses on nests he has the merit for.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i><b>Arcane Blood</b></i><br /> Much too strong, this basically removes the need to hunt entirely. At the very least I'd limit it to once a week, or better tie to to existing feeding. Something like, &quot;When the vampire feeds she draws additional power from the nest. The first [nest dots] points of damage she deals while feeding yield double the vitae. She can benefit from no more than [Nest Dots] additional vitae in this way each week.&quot;<br /> That changes the power from 'vampire never leaves nest' to 'vampire invites people into her nest' while makes for more interesting narrative possibilities. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, this is my bad, I originally thought Herd was per day; I was making it equivalent to that. I'll set it to per week, but I don't want to break the thematic of the Kindred learning to subsist on the Nest directly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><i>Lair of the Beast</i></b><br /> I'd shift the lair buffing functions of dot two here. Give the vampire what is essentially a lair frenzy, that causes the entire Nest to side with him (increasing all relevant Nest pools by his Blood Potency). That puts more focus on the whole &quot;my nest is better than yours&quot; and avoids crossover with the Coil of the Wyrm. </div> </div> </div>I like that idea, I'll poke at that. This does mean I need to be sure the second dot is, well, worth a second dot, though, without that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><i>Master of the Domain</i></b><br /> I like it generally, but wonder if there isn't a way to differentiate it from Animalism 5 (which has many of the same effects). </div> </div> </div>Ah, I'd forgotten about Animalism's 5th dot, as I rarely use the discipline. As it is, though, the only crossover there is the extension of the senses, and it's not quite as powerful in the COil (though of course it's also an automatic ability, no need to re-mark territory). If you have suggestions, though, I'm glad to hear them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><i>Scales</i></b><br /> On the whole I like all of these. The first one struck me as strange, but strange is the dominion of scales. Love the procedures too, they nailed the whole &quot;crazed sorcerer's evil house&quot; feel I expected of the Mystery. Bravo there. </div> </div> </div> Thanks!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T14:25:58-07:00","id":449768,"title":"","content":"I love this so much I'm going to use it in my personal LARP. Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My horror roleplaying blog with a strong focus on World of Darkness and Call of Cthulhu can be found here: <a href=\"http://stwildonroleplaying.blogspot.com.au/\" target=\"_blank\">http://stwildonroleplaying.blogspot.com.au/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1248-laraqua","name":"Laraqua","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T14:52:10-07:00","id":449798,"title":"","content":"Glad you like it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}